+\subsection{Explanatory Analyses}
+After prediction-level exports are written, two additional analyses speak to RQ3 without changing stratum definitions or official training files. First, a KC-level confounding analysis (Section~\ref{sec:a4_confounding}) relates ECE to training-only covariates (frequency, a difficulty proxy, item support, learner exposure, and a curriculum-position proxy). These associations are observational. Second, a controlled sparsification experiment (Appendix~\ref{app:a9_sparsify}) downsamples training rows of originally dense KCs while holding the test set, labels, KC identifiers, and all other KCs fixed, then retrains DKT and SimpleKT. That experiment tests whether reducing training count for the \emph{same} KC is followed by a within-KC ECE increase; it does not identify a causal law for real-world sparsity.
